cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use arcwind, please cite it using the metadata below, and cite Louvet et al. (2018), whose method it implements."
title: "arcwind: Analysis of Resolved Conical Winds In Nascent Disks"
abstract: >-
  arcwind measures the geometry and kinematics of protoplanetary disk winds
  from transverse position-velocity diagrams of resolved line cubes. It extracts
  the wind's emission in cuts perpendicular to its axis and fits a conical wind
  model (opening angle, launch radius, poloidal velocity law and rotation) to all
  cuts at once, at any inclination, with model comparison and bootstrap
  uncertainties.
type: software
